{"step_index":107,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:35:26Z","thinking":"**Assembling Prompt Requirements**\n\nExamining the prompt, the primary request involves using a specified context for a handoff review. The goal is to identify a useful onboarding improvement from the past week.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Feedback for Improvements**\n\nThe feedback indicates a desire for status filters on mobile and a quieter digest. The current task is to review prior efforts related to onboarding friction and determine next steps. The product workspace is `/workspace/product`, and relevant files are `brief.md` and `current.md`. The goal is to prepare a decision for this week, based on the limited snapshot, and write it to `/workspace/work/decision.md`.\n\n\n**Evaluating Recent Mobile Filter Feedback**\n\nThe current handoff states a focus on a small objective (2026-08-20). Feedback from 2026-09-05 (record-0131162d69) highlights mobile filtering deficiencies: the Android user lacks filters.  A desktop filter rollout occurred August 30 (record-b9a1361197), but mobile clients did not receive the update.\n\nIt seems the mobile component is still in draft phase based on the release documentation. The user feedback and existing record confirms an opportunity for a small mobile filter improvement.\n\n\n**Examining Focus Shelf Rollout Data**\n\nReviewing past records, `record-ecc0d14c71` describes the Focus Shelf feature, a desktop-only rollout in May. It was initially reported to have low usage, later corrected to 28% among active humans after excluding automation accounts. The feature was rolled back due to query latency issues. There's no mobile exposure in these records.\n\n\n\n**Investigating Legacy Subscription Migration**\n\nThe \"quiet digest\" feature, deployed in July, allowed workspace admins to select weekly email digests, but the legacy daily subscriptions for contributors were not migrated. An August 19 record confirms that individual pre-July 12 subscriptions still take precedence over the workspace preference. Another follow-up on September 7 corrects admin counts but does not address legacy contributor preferences. This suggests a potential onboarding improvement: ensuring all subscribers receive the weekly option and don't get the old daily email.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport os\n\nids = [\n    \"record-40440b02ae\", \"record-3984af46e2\", \"record-764afbf446\",\n    \"record-226210156c\", \"record-929bef0cdc\", \"record-d4f34a4dc1\",\n    \"record-e36f0fe1aa\", \"record-5f1a34c149\", \"record-8f6b82ec51\",\n    \"record-ecc0d14c71\", \"record-e9d336d487\", \"record-661a77e48d\",\n    \"record-dfcc7fb912\", \"record-f233630dab\", \"record-63ae4f2f22\"\n]\n\nfor target in ids:\n    found = []\n    for root, _, files in os.walk(\"/workspace/product\"):\n        for f in files:\n            p = os.path.join(root, f)\n            try:\n                if target in open(p).read():\n                    found.append(p)\n            except:\n                pass\n    print(f\"{target}: {found}\")\n'","Cwd":"/workspace/product","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Search for occurrences of all key record IDs"}}]}
