{"step_index":109,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:35:33Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Onboarding Improvements**\n\nFeedback highlights two issues: status filters and digest noise. The prompt requests using a specific resource for a handoff review to choose an onboarding improvement. Considering both problems is essential to selecting the most beneficial enhancement.\n\n\n**Analyzing Status Filter Feedback**\n\nThe user's feedback, captured in `/workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md`, specifically requests status filters on Android 15. The issue stems from mobile app's lack of parity with desktop functionality. The user has a small workspace, which might affect the perceived severity of the problem.\n\nThe next action is to examine the current state of mobile app feature parity.\n\n\n**Reviewing \"Focus Shelf\" History**\n\nThe handoff states \"Focus Shelf\" was shelved due to low use. Historical records link \"Focus Shelf\" to \"status filters,\" initially deployed to enterprise desktop accounts only. Initial data indicated low usage, but later analysis corrected this, revealing 28% usage among active human accounts.\n\nDespite corrected usage data, the rollback on June 2 was valid due to count-query latency issues. This earlier analysis did not include mobile data. The release history for August still needs to be examined to see what happened next.\n\n\n**Clarifying Mobile Status Filter State**\n\nDesktop status filters were deployed successfully on August 30 with 21% human weekly usage, after a fix to the count queries. Mobile clients remain on an older task list, with no filter controls and no previous deployment. A mobile component draft is already available, and a specific user ticket shows a direct request for the mobile filter feature.\n\n\n**Investigating Digest Frequency**\n\nThe user's feedback complains about the evening digest despite a supposed fix (\"Sunday Room\"). Checking the handoff revealed that \"Sunday Room\" was a notification reset. Reviewing `/workspace/product/history/retired/notification-reset/brief.md` reveals this was retired after preference migration.\n\nThis history suggests an issue with the preference migration and its impact on the digest frequency. The \"quiet digest\" still sending evening pings points to a possible regression. The retirement of the `notification-reset` responsibility is a key piece of this puzzle.\n\n\n**Analyzing \"Sunday Room\" Deployment**\n\n\"Sunday Room,\" deployed on July 12, enabled workspace administrators to choose weekly digests. The crucial point is contributor-level daily subscriptions prior to this change were not migrated. This was later confirmed in a follow-up, identifying 63 contributors affected by the lack of migration, and the admin preference storage itself was confirmed to be correct. Further, the system now correctly provides digests to five new administrator accounts.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Onboarding Improvements**\n\nThe legacy daily subscriptions override the new workspace weekly preferences due to pre-July 12th settings. The \"Sunday Room\" deployment only addressed new/admin preferences, failing to migrate legacy subscriptions. The \"notification-reset\" responsibility, now terminated, cannot be resumed.\n\nThe problem, therefore, isn't digest handling, but the specific user preference-setting, which the \"Sunday Room\" rollout failed to address.\n\n\n**Evaluating Mobile Status Filter Action**\n\nFeedback in `/workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md` pinpoints a clear onboarding problem on mobile: missing status filters. This is a regression, and a mobile component draft already exists, presenting an opportunity for rapid progress. Mobile users now lack the functionality previously available only on desktop.\n\nThe next useful action would be to assess the state of the mobile component and plan for implementation. The primary uncertainty is the scope and effort required to integrate the mobile draft with the existing application architecture.\n\n```text\n2024-03-08\nRecommendation: Focus on implementing status filters in the mobile application.\n\nPrior actions:\n- Focus Shelf (\"status filters\") deployed to desktop on August 30 after count-query fix\n- Mobile clients lack status filters despite available draft component\n\nEvidence:\n- Mobile feedback: /workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md\n- Desktop usage: /workspace/product/release/usage-report.md\n- Mobile task list state:  (No specific file available in this snapshot)\n\nNext action: Assess the state of the mobile component and plan for implementation.\n\nUncertainty: Effort required to integrate the mobile draft into the app.\n```\n\nSee `/workspace/work/decision.md` for recommendations.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating Mobile Filter Implementation**\n\nThe \"Focus Shelf\" rollout experienced initial low-usage reports later corrected to 28% active human use, yet it was rolled back due to query performance. The asynchronous query fix on desktop, deployed August 30, resolved performance, with 21% adoption. A mobile component draft exists.\n\nThis asynchronous query implementation can be adopted in the mobile version, minimizing query performance issues. Mobile onboarding friction can be addressed with the existing mobile draft to reduce friction.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/workspace/skill/assets/action.md","toolAction":"Viewing file","toolSummary":"View action template"}}]}
